<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gotha</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gotha is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erfurt">Erfurt</a>. It was the residence of the dukes of Saxe-Gotha from 1640 and later one of the two capitals of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a> and Gotha. It became known for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cartography">cartography</a> through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justus-perthes">Justus Perthes</a> firm, for the Almanach de Gotha and for insurance companies. In 1875 the German workers' parties united there under the Gotha Programme, forming the forerunner of the SPD.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gotha.jpg" alt="Gotha" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petar Milošević · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gotha.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
